WEBVTT

00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:06.650
It's said that superior combat vessels must take on risks

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:09.900
that match the capabilities of the vessel.

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:14.220
People also say that the Nadesico is the greatest combat vessel

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:15.990
in the arsenal of the United Earth Armed Forces.

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:18.080
That's why we are here

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:19.360
in the midst of the fighting.

00:01:52.910 --> 00:01:56.180
The Nadesico was placed at the forefront of the UEAF assault,

00:01:56.180 --> 00:02:00.560
and the enemy singled us out as if we had killed their parents.

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:03.810
If that's how they're going to play,

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:05.750
then we're not going to hold anything back!

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:10.100
The prosperity of our nation always hinges on our gallantry!

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:12.100
Yeah...

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:13.350
Hup, hup!

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:14.600
They won't get me!

00:02:14.990 --> 00:02:16.350
Time to earn my pay.

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:23.370
All Aestivalis have taken off.

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:23.830
Those "Unforgettable Days"

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:25.220
All units, start engaging the enemy!

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:27.410
Those "Unforgettable Days"

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:29.040
All right, here we go!

00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:33.190
What?!

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:36.710
What the...

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:39.550
What?

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:49.820
Damn lizard tailed bastards! All hands abandon ship!

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:52.250
All rounds were from the Nadesico!

00:02:52.250 --> 00:02:53.310
What?!

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:55.630
Those bastards!

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:02.340
What? What's happening?

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:05.130
Our Aestivalis are shooting at friendly ships.

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:06.950
Shooting at friendlies?

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:10.190
Attack guidance system shows no malfunctions.

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:13.660
The Nadesico's Aestivalis are attacking enemy units.

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:15.540
But our enemy is over there!

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:19.840
Nadesico's Aestivalis are attacking both enemy and UEAF units!

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.700
Why?!

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:23.470
Cease fire immediately!

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:24.620
The enemy is close at hand.

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:27.340
If we ease our fire now, we may be decimated.

00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:31.980
Jeez, only Jovians! Attack only the Jovians!

00:03:32.630 --> 00:03:34.970
We're trying to engage the enemy!

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:37.180
So, why does this keep on happening?

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:41.990
Hey, what are we going to do now?

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:44.160
We have to do what we have to do.

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:50.120
What the hell are you doing?!

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:56.460
I guess the bright side is that no one is attacking the Nadesico.

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:59.290
In any case, everyone watch your own back.

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:01.830
Send out more Aestivalis for reinforcements.

00:04:01.830 --> 00:04:02.970
We have no more pilots.

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:05.140
I'll go.

00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:06.800
This is my time to shine!

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:11.940
Aiding the Captain is the duty of the executive officer.

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:13.520
No, there's more to this!

00:04:13.930 --> 00:04:16.550
Yurika! I want to protect you.

00:04:17.030 --> 00:04:17.980
Yurika!

00:04:25.690 --> 00:04:28.270
Jun-san! Please come in, Jun-san!

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:40.600
The fighting that day was a terrible mess.

00:04:43.790 --> 00:04:48.500
The Jovians became confused with an enemy that shot at both sides,

00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:50.490
and they quickly ceased hostilities and withdrew.

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:54.730
The UEAF also pulled out having had enough of indiscriminate attacks from the Nadesico.

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:57.230
Well in any case, I'm just glad everyone made it back safely.

00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:06.660
Looks like the Aestivalis suffered only minor dents and scratches.

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:09.370
Oh man, this one sure is beat up good!

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:13.160
Jun, why were you piloting that one?

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:17.010
What is it? What do you want to say?

00:05:17.470 --> 00:05:19.330
I think he's using block signs.

00:05:19.330 --> 00:05:23.090
"With the Nadesico undermanned, it's the XO's job to fill in."

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:26.800
Well, that's fine, but make sure to wear the pilot suit when you do.

00:05:29.320 --> 00:05:30.180
What is he saying?

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:33.290
He says "For service to Yurika-san..."

00:05:33.290 --> 00:05:36.730
Doing this for Yurika is fine, but you have to put on your pilot suit.

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:41.310
"I don't want to start bickering with you at a time like this."

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:44.290
Yes, yes. I think that's enough of that.

00:05:46.510 --> 00:05:47.240
What was that?

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:51.410
"Make sure to put on your seatbelt when you get in an Aestivalis."

00:05:52.530 --> 00:05:55.040
I think he's fine besides the whiplash in his neck.

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:57.200
But he won't be able to speak normally for a while.

00:05:58.780 --> 00:06:01.790
Again, no dialogs for me.

00:06:01.790 --> 00:06:04.800
I just want to say,

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:07.750
how much I love Yurika.

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:08.950
Baka.

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:11.600
Take care of yourself, Jun-kun.

00:06:12.060 --> 00:06:14.930
Thank God no one was fatally injured in all of this, but...

00:06:15.410 --> 00:06:18.140
Do you have any idea how much these battleships costs?!

00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:20.320
Hey, that's the one I sank.

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:24.930
That ship, the Foxglove, cost more to build than the Nadesico.

00:06:25.470 --> 00:06:27.630
I shot down fifty.

00:06:27.630 --> 00:06:29.500
That's pretty good, coming from you.

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:30.810
But...

00:06:30.810 --> 00:06:31.400
But?

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:34.730
Everything I shot down had the United Earth insignia on it.

00:06:34.730 --> 00:06:37.090
Please stop!

00:06:37.490 --> 00:06:39.660
No simple "buts" will be enough for an excuse.

00:06:40.110 --> 00:06:43.480
I'll say the number of units I shot down.
It was seventy-eight.

00:06:43.480 --> 00:06:45.180
Includes friendly and enemy.

00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:46.810
Sixty-two were friendly!

00:06:47.220 --> 00:06:47.670
Oh, really?

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:52.010
Akito, you've been awfully quiet.

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:54.260
Well...

00:06:54.710 --> 00:06:56.320
I wasn't as bad as either of you.

00:06:56.320 --> 00:07:00.430
I was aiming for the enemy's Chulip,
but I ended up destroying the UEAF's refueling depot.

00:07:03.390 --> 00:07:05.860
Do you have any idea how much it cost to build that depot?

00:07:06.450 --> 00:07:09.100
Aren't they all covered by insurance?

00:07:09.100 --> 00:07:13.550
Of course, but we'll still have to make compensatory payments.

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:18.020
In any case, thank heavens there was no loss of life from this.

00:07:18.390 --> 00:07:21.530
I shudder to think how much more we'd have had to pay.

00:07:21.530 --> 00:07:23.710
We did have one suffer from whiplash.

00:07:25.510 --> 00:07:28.490
So? How did this end up happening?

00:07:28.490 --> 00:07:30.590
Why did we end up attacking the UEAF?

00:07:30.980 --> 00:07:32.990
It wasn't like I was trying to attack them.

00:07:32.990 --> 00:07:35.380
We all dearly love our blue mother Earth.

00:07:35.380 --> 00:07:37.560
We would never betray the UEAF.

00:07:37.970 --> 00:07:39.700
Then was it because of faulty maintenance?

00:07:40.190 --> 00:07:42.720
I'm not going to sit here and listen to you blame us.

00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:45.400
You're questioning our safe and accurate maintenance?

00:07:45.880 --> 00:07:48.810
We've been fighting constantly. It could have been a careless error.

00:07:49.480 --> 00:07:52.660
We can't just write off the fatigue the maintenance crew faces.

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:56.740
Rested or wasted, people die when maintenance screws up.

00:07:56.930 --> 00:08:00.830
People's lives are at stake with maintenance. You hear me?!

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:04.170
I may screw up with women, but I never botch up fixing equipment!

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:07.560
Don't blame your sorry ass shortcomings on us!

00:08:07.560 --> 00:08:08.500
Please wait a moment.

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:12.420
There's no indication the pilots or the maintenance crew are at fault.

00:08:12.850 --> 00:08:14.340
Then what's the cause?

00:08:14.860 --> 00:08:18.760
A UEAF research ship is heading our way to investigate the cause.

00:08:19.400 --> 00:08:24.560
They say the Nadesico's defensive computer is suspected.

00:08:28.990 --> 00:08:32.150
No, please stop! That's not an enemy!

00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:42.420
Don't look at me! I didn't do anything!

00:08:42.420 --> 00:08:45.330
The escape pod from the research ship is requesting assistance.

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:52.630
Hey, an attack order's been issued again.

00:08:53.250 --> 00:08:54.770
Who is issuing the command?

00:08:54.770 --> 00:08:55.880
I have no idea.

00:08:57.850 --> 00:08:59.800
Don't fire at that. That's not the enemy.

00:09:00.110 --> 00:09:03.060
UEAF research vessel pod coming aboard.

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:14.910
The investigators fired upon were predictably not at all calm.

00:09:15.330 --> 00:09:18.200
They started nit-picking at all the faults of the Nadesico.

00:09:18.880 --> 00:09:21.610
Interesting how people revel in condemning others' shortcomings.

00:09:23.430 --> 00:09:26.960
Computers have the capacity to learn, it goes without saying.

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:29.050
Computers accumulate knowledge from experience

00:09:29.050 --> 00:09:31.000
and take the best possible option at any given time.

00:09:32.120 --> 00:09:33.700
The Nadesico's computer...

00:09:33.700 --> 00:09:34.630
It's Omoikane.

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:37.050
Oh, that's the name of the computer.

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:40.610
Attaching names to computers, which are mere tools,

00:09:40.610 --> 00:09:42.750
is a bad practice from the late 20th century.

00:09:42.750 --> 00:09:44.560
But Omoikane is Omoikane.

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:47.100
Note: Omoikane = Heavy Bell // Karuikane = Light Bell
I don't care if it's Omoikane or Karuikane.

00:09:47.820 --> 00:09:51.810
Nadesico's computer remembers breaching Earth's defenses.

00:09:54.110 --> 00:09:58.320
Through that it learned that, to the Nadesico,
the UEAF acts as an obstacle, making them its enemy.

00:09:58.960 --> 00:10:02.890
This causes it to show negativity when working with the UEAF.

00:10:04.930 --> 00:10:08.240
Put in human terms, it's as if a business acquired their rival,

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:10.910
then started overworking their former competitors.

00:10:10.910 --> 00:10:13.000
That's a very well put analogy.

00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:16.050
I can sympathize. I know how that feels!

00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:19.180
If it were human, too much stress would make it go haywire.

00:10:19.880 --> 00:10:22.250
In the case of computers, the system would freeze up.

00:10:22.650 --> 00:10:24.090
If it were mere lock up,

00:10:24.090 --> 00:10:26.980
we could simply remove the buggy data, and reset the system.

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:30.150
Omoikane has an automatic reset built-in.

00:10:30.490 --> 00:10:34.820
The resentment it learned against the UEAF is too strong.

00:10:35.310 --> 00:10:37.660
Each time it reboots, the stress increases.

00:10:37.660 --> 00:10:40.740
It has culminated with the hostile action it took this time.

00:10:41.270 --> 00:10:44.160
The solution lies with totally erasing what it has learned so far.

00:10:44.830 --> 00:10:46.820
We'll have to install a new program.

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:48.830
Could I interject, please?

00:10:48.830 --> 00:10:49.340
Yes?

00:10:50.380 --> 00:10:52.660
How can such extreme measures be tolerated?

00:10:53.270 --> 00:11:01.500
If we do that, the knowledge it's gained of how to fight the enemy through the conflict on Mars will be lost.

00:11:02.040 --> 00:11:04.780
The Nadesico is part of the UEAF.

00:11:04.780 --> 00:11:08.100
The memories it gathered are far more trouble than they're worth.

00:11:08.730 --> 00:11:13.260
Besides, humans are the ones who fight to protect the Earth.

00:11:13.580 --> 00:11:14.440
Not machines.

00:11:14.830 --> 00:11:18.370
It goes without saying that the Nadesico belongs to the UEAF.

00:11:18.370 --> 00:11:20.900
It must forget all it learned when it was hostile to the UEAF.

00:11:21.610 --> 00:11:23.510
It must forget everything to learn anew.

00:11:23.950 --> 00:11:26.330
That's the rationale of adults, isn't it?

00:11:26.940 --> 00:11:30.120
That we should just forget things that are inconvenient to remember.

00:11:31.130 --> 00:11:32.680
Adults are deceitful.

00:11:34.640 --> 00:11:35.410
Ruri-chan...

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:38.250
Omoikane

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:51.250
What the hell?! Why are they all dressed the same?!

00:11:51.250 --> 00:11:51.670
Hey you!

00:11:52.640 --> 00:11:53.120
Nadesico, Computer Control Room

00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:55.260
Switch control to auxiliary computer!

00:11:55.260 --> 00:11:55.650
Nadesico, Computer Control Room

00:11:55.650 --> 00:11:56.810
Start the installation!
Nadesico, Computer Control Room

00:11:56.810 --> 00:11:56.820
Start the installation!

00:11:59.150 --> 00:12:02.250
Do we really have to erase all the data?

00:12:02.560 --> 00:12:03.810
I'm afraid so!

00:12:03.810 --> 00:12:04.590
Yes, yes!

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:09.490
We will rewrite Omoikane into an absolutely obedient program, thus the Nadesico will be reborn!

00:12:09.780 --> 00:12:12.460
That's right, from civilian ship to a true battleship.

00:12:12.800 --> 00:12:14.410
It'll be turned into a ship for the military.

00:12:17.600 --> 00:12:19.000
Akito!

00:12:19.780 --> 00:12:21.700
What'd you do that for?!

00:12:21.700 --> 00:12:23.280
Well, I have a favor to ask.

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:26.300
Could you PLEASE come with me for a while?

00:12:26.390 --> 00:12:28.140
No thanks!

00:12:28.140 --> 00:12:28.720
Why not?

00:12:29.320 --> 00:12:32.000
I still haven't given up on my dream to become a cook.

00:12:32.310 --> 00:12:35.120
I'm devoting myself to practicing cooking when I'm not fighting.

00:12:35.120 --> 00:12:37.520
But we need the help of an Aestivalis pilot.

00:12:37.550 --> 00:12:40.780
There are many others. There's Ryoko, Hikaru, lzumi, Akatsu...

00:12:40.780 --> 00:12:41.800
That won't work.

00:12:43.210 --> 00:12:45.220
It has to be you, Tenkawa-san.

00:12:45.700 --> 00:12:46.780
Please help us.

00:12:47.100 --> 00:12:48.410
You heard the girl.

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:50.910
Uribatake Seiya

00:12:51.300 --> 00:12:52.920
This stinks!

00:12:52.920 --> 00:12:54.160
You'll get used to it.

00:12:54.610 --> 00:12:56.670
Are men's bedrooms all like this?

00:12:56.670 --> 00:12:57.830
I don't like this room.

00:12:57.890 --> 00:12:59.250
What can we do?

00:12:59.250 --> 00:13:01.060
The control room is occupied,

00:13:01.060 --> 00:13:03.540
and we can't do something this shady on the bridge.

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:05.980
Hey, watch out there! I'm working on that figurine!

00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:11.490
This "debugging," you can do that from here?

00:13:12.550 --> 00:13:16.310
It just so happens that I've accessed Omoikane several times.

00:13:16.740 --> 00:13:19.730
The program is so well written just watching it at work is enough.

00:13:19.730 --> 00:13:20.150
Here we go!

00:13:21.750 --> 00:13:22.710
It's adorable!

00:13:23.030 --> 00:13:24.350
An Aestivalis?

00:13:24.350 --> 00:13:25.740
The graphic representation of one.

00:13:26.470 --> 00:13:30.510
It dives into the Omoikane code, hunts breakdowns and fixes them.

00:13:30.510 --> 00:13:33.660
Sort of like a superhero janitor of cyberspace.

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:35.080
But why...

00:13:35.810 --> 00:13:38.410
What? You got a problem with my tastes?!

00:13:38.720 --> 00:13:42.330
By controlling the simulator that's hooked up to my host system,

00:13:42.330 --> 00:13:44.950
you'll become a righteous cyber warrior!

00:13:45.480 --> 00:13:47.430
I'll be backing him up.

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:48.430
Much obliged.

00:13:49.010 --> 00:13:50.350
Time to get cracking!

00:13:50.870 --> 00:13:52.550
Tenkawa Aesti, online!

00:13:52.550 --> 00:13:53.260
Sure...

00:14:00.640 --> 00:14:02.750
This is the inside of a computer?

00:14:06.790 --> 00:14:11.560
That's my graphical representation of the memory core.

00:14:11.920 --> 00:14:16.060
I remember the library at MIT, where I failed to get in seven times.

00:14:16.060 --> 00:14:17.460
So, where am I supposed to go?

00:14:17.750 --> 00:14:19.400
I'll be your guide.

00:14:19.400 --> 00:14:20.160
You're in charge then.

00:14:20.600 --> 00:14:21.700
Oh, go up here.

00:14:23.490 --> 00:14:24.070
Go right.

00:14:24.980 --> 00:14:25.510
Now straight.

00:14:26.270 --> 00:14:28.420
Our destination is Omoikane's self-consciousness.

00:14:32.470 --> 00:14:35.310
That's the military's new program installing itself.

00:14:36.140 --> 00:14:37.800
Guess it's time to send it home.

00:14:37.800 --> 00:14:38.510
Not yet.

00:14:39.230 --> 00:14:41.520
If we attack the new program now,

00:14:41.640 --> 00:14:46.030
the installation will stop, and the Nadesico will still defy the UEAF.

00:14:46.660 --> 00:14:47.950
Then what do we do?

00:14:48.260 --> 00:14:49.610
We'll move on ahead.

00:14:49.610 --> 00:14:51.950
Please head to where Omoikane's self-consciousness is located.

00:14:52.290 --> 00:14:52.910
Roger!

00:14:54.630 --> 00:14:55.490
This isn't right.

00:14:55.970 --> 00:14:57.910
You're kind, aren't you, Tenkawa-san?

00:14:58.770 --> 00:14:59.450
Quit it.

00:15:02.520 --> 00:15:03.110
That's...

00:15:03.580 --> 00:15:05.490
That's where Omoikane's self-consciousness resides.

00:15:05.820 --> 00:15:08.480
It's a testament to what makes the Nadesico, the Nadesico.

00:15:09.050 --> 00:15:10.930
It's a testament of one's longing to be one's own self.

00:15:11.500 --> 00:15:13.340
A testament of longing to be yourself?

00:15:13.680 --> 00:15:15.480
Memories that are important to you.

00:15:16.100 --> 00:15:19.490
Precious memories you can't sweep aside even if you want to.

00:15:19.990 --> 00:15:24.560
Remembrance. Memories you can't sweep aside even if you want to.

00:15:26.240 --> 00:15:28.200
Testament to what makes you yourself?

00:15:28.200 --> 00:15:30.860
Let Omoikane forget for a short while.

00:15:31.420 --> 00:15:32.640
Forget?

00:15:33.220 --> 00:15:34.110
Look carefully.

00:15:35.060 --> 00:15:36.920
See that branch that extends out?

00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:39.540
Please cut those flowers off.

00:15:40.550 --> 00:15:43.990
It's heart-wrenching, but the branches will grow again.

00:15:44.700 --> 00:15:46.820
Then Omoikane will remember once again,

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:51.200
and the Nadesico can continue to be the Nadesico.

00:15:52.060 --> 00:15:52.690
I understand.

00:15:53.250 --> 00:15:55.570
Omoikane, let yourself forget,

00:15:56.620 --> 00:15:58.020
and please become an adult.

00:15:59.030 --> 00:16:02.900
If you can pretend to be obedient to the UEAF,

00:16:02.900 --> 00:16:04.790
then the Nadesico will be able to continue to be the Nadesico.

00:16:09.390 --> 00:16:11.070
Is this really working?

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:15.030
Akito!

00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:17.630
What's wrong, Akito?!

00:16:17.630 --> 00:16:18.950
There it is.

00:16:20.550 --> 00:16:21.710
What was that?

00:16:22.010 --> 00:16:24.120
That's the xenophobic consciousness of the computer.

00:16:24.490 --> 00:16:26.210
Omoikane's reflex for self-preservation!

00:16:27.440 --> 00:16:29.910
It's the energy within that wants to remember what it holds dear.

00:16:32.020 --> 00:16:33.680
Damn! What's going on here?

00:16:35.520 --> 00:16:36.010
What?!

00:16:36.440 --> 00:16:38.270
Gekiganger Three!

00:16:39.150 --> 00:16:39.890
It can't be.

00:16:40.400 --> 00:16:45.900
Omoikane thinks of this as the most powerful and righteous entity

00:16:46.370 --> 00:16:49.790
it has encountered, making it the vanguard of justice and its ally.

00:16:50.410 --> 00:16:54.800
Omoikane's been watching the Gekiganger videos along with you.

00:16:55.600 --> 00:16:58.570
That's no reason why it has to be Gekiganger!

00:16:58.880 --> 00:17:02.710
Tenkawa-san, you know Gekiganger like no one else does. Please...

00:17:02.710 --> 00:17:05.080
You're asking me to fight Gekiganger?!

00:17:05.420 --> 00:17:06.400
Please, I beg you.

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:09.800
Do it, Akito! You can easily cut down an oaf like Gekiganger!

00:17:09.800 --> 00:17:10.820
What was that?!

00:17:10.820 --> 00:17:12.740
Please, you must defeat it!

00:17:13.170 --> 00:17:14.340
That's easy to say, but...

00:17:14.740 --> 00:17:17.160
Well, it doesn't look like it's going to let you off the hook.

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:20.000
Gekigan Beam!

00:17:20.000 --> 00:17:20.750
Damn!

00:17:22.660 --> 00:17:24.430
Gekigan Cutter!

00:17:31.050 --> 00:17:34.610
This is nuts! I can't defeat Gekiganger!

00:17:34.610 --> 00:17:36.400
You can! Tenkawa-san, I'm sure you can.

00:17:36.990 --> 00:17:40.200
Your attachment to that robot is stronger than Omoikane's.

00:17:40.680 --> 00:17:43.030
My attachment?

00:17:44.810 --> 00:17:45.290
My

00:17:46.770 --> 00:17:48.460
Gekiganger!

00:17:54.520 --> 00:17:55.670
We're evenly matched for power.

00:17:57.100 --> 00:17:58.590
Gekigan Beam!

00:18:01.480 --> 00:18:03.770
Gekigan Kick!

00:18:09.720 --> 00:18:11.450
This is going nowhere.

00:18:11.450 --> 00:18:14.800
Actually, the odds are against us because a human is piloting!

00:18:15.390 --> 00:18:16.320
No, they aren't!

00:18:17.470 --> 00:18:23.030
Tenkawa-san has known the robot for so long, and loved it so much more than Omoikane.

00:18:23.510 --> 00:18:25.660
Akito-san's strong affection can't be defeated!

00:18:26.030 --> 00:18:28.500
I like how you put that.

00:18:28.990 --> 00:18:31.640
For so long ago, I have loved it so much.

00:18:32.350 --> 00:18:32.980
Yes!

00:18:36.690 --> 00:18:37.680
Did you know?

00:18:39.440 --> 00:18:43.090
In episode 28, Gekiganger becomes Gekiganger V.

00:18:44.860 --> 00:18:48.270
Do you know the legendary transformation sequence, Dragon Gangar?!

00:18:59.240 --> 00:19:01.330
Dragon Blast!

00:19:11.900 --> 00:19:14.830
Self-preservation reflex is gone. Memory correction complete.

00:19:15.270 --> 00:19:18.120
Now all that's left is the new program, Tenkawa-san.

00:19:18.120 --> 00:19:20.070
At this rate, everything will be erased.

00:19:22.490 --> 00:19:24.480
But is this a good idea?

00:19:24.480 --> 00:19:26.640
We don't want them to find out we're doing this, right?

00:19:26.640 --> 00:19:28.280
Don't worry about it!

00:19:28.280 --> 00:19:32.020
I'm feeding the investigators' computers dummy data.

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:34.270
It's all yours to blast away, Akito!

00:19:34.570 --> 00:19:35.340
Roger that!

00:19:43.470 --> 00:19:47.100
Dragon Gangar was only on paper, and was never featured on TV.

00:19:47.590 --> 00:19:50.540
I only found out about it going through Gai's Roman albums.

00:19:51.330 --> 00:19:52.210
Thank you.

00:19:53.330 --> 00:19:56.170
I'm taken aback at how strongly attached you are to what you love.

00:19:58.230 --> 00:20:00.170
That was pretty interesting.

00:20:01.870 --> 00:20:02.810
Thank you.

00:20:04.700 --> 00:20:07.770
After that, it appeared no abnormalities manifested

00:20:07.770 --> 00:20:11.690
from either Omoikane, nor from the Nadesico itself.

00:20:12.380 --> 00:20:16.770
Beautiful, beautiful! Earth will win this war!

00:20:16.770 --> 00:20:17.730
Right, Captain?

00:20:18.220 --> 00:20:19.750
Yes, of course!

00:20:19.750 --> 00:20:21.240
Well, let's take off.

00:20:21.690 --> 00:20:21.940
Yes, Sir!

00:20:22.840 --> 00:20:27.790
Slow speed ahead, right full rudder!

00:20:30.820 --> 00:20:32.320
Living Now

00:20:32.320 --> 00:20:33.820
for Those
Living Now

00:20:33.820 --> 00:20:35.530
Unforgettable Days
for Those
Living Now

00:20:37.170 --> 00:20:38.670
Yes, that's right.

00:21:45.880 --> 00:21:48.460
Breath-taking speed! Exciting adventures!

00:21:48.460 --> 00:21:50.230
When Akito says his farewell to Yurika,

00:21:50.230 --> 00:21:52.160
the barrier between illusion and reality comes crashing down.

00:21:52.360 --> 00:21:56.950
A heartwarming classic fit to be the mid-series climax is born.

00:21:56.950 --> 00:21:59.460
A deluxe flashy epic with a rainbow assortment of action.

00:21:59.490 --> 00:22:01.800
A momentous saga aimed at all good children and their mothers.

00:22:01.800 --> 00:22:04.210
The series that's the talk of the workplace, the school, the home.

00:22:04.210 --> 00:22:08.000
Next Martian Successor Nadesico: "There is No Single Truth"

00:22:08.000 --> 00:22:10.120
Let's watch it, everyone!
